{
  "_comment": [
    "Argon2id PHC strings both backends must read the same way (BOOTSTRAP.md §5.1, issue #16).",
    "`verifies`: minted by each backend, at the §5.1 cost and at another, so verification is proven in both",
    "directions and is shown to read the cost from the string rather than from the current constants.",
    "`rejects`: each must answer 'does not verify' in both backends - never an error, a panic or a 500.",
    "The accepted shape is exactly $argon2id$v=19$m=<n>,t=<n>,p=<n>$<salt>$<hash>: unpadded standard base64,",
    "8*p <= m <= 65536 (KiB), 1 <= t <= 10, 1 <= p <= 255, a hash of at least 4 bytes, and neither base64",
    "segment of a length that cannot decode (1 mod 4). The m and t ceilings are #68's, headroom over the",
    "operating cost (m=19456, t=2) rather than BouncyCastle's own 2^24 KiB / Go's absent ceiling.",
    "A reject row that tests a shape rule carries the tag a lenient parser would compute for the parameters",
    "it reads, so only the rule refuses it, not a tag mismatch. `minted_by` names what computed the tag:",
    "go (x/crypto/argon2), bouncycastle (Argon2BytesGenerator, for what x/crypto cannot express), or absent",
    "where no tag can be computed. Each backend's suite recomputes the tags it can mint, so a tag that stops",
    "being genuine fails there. Regenerate an entry by minting it, never by editing the tag."
  ],
